.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH PIDP8I 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pidp8i \- control the PiDP-8/I simulator user service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pidp8i
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pidp8i
is the operator front end for the simulator on a PiDP-8/I cabinet. It
wraps the
.BR systemd (1)
user service
.IR pidp8i.service ,
so you do not have to type the canonical
.B "systemctl --user"
form: a verb such as
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.B restart
or
.B status
is passed through as
.BI "systemctl --user " command
.B pidp8i .
.PP
The session itself runs inside
.BR screen (1)
(the console manager named in
.IR /etc/pidp8i/pidp8i.rc ;
tmux is the alternative), which keeps the simulator console reachable
after the SSH session that started it is gone.
.PP
Start and stop have panel semantics beyond plain unit control: the
front-panel switches are scanned first (via
.BR scanswitch ),
so the STOP switch can veto a start and the boot-selector switches can
pick which script from
.IR /usr/share/pidp8i/boot
the simulator boots when it comes up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B install
Upstream helper that copies the user unit into
.I ~/.local/share/systemd/user
and enables it; packaged for parity with
.BR "make install" ,
not normally needed: the RPM ships the unit in
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user
and
.B "systemctl --user enable pidp8i"
does the rest.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/pidp8i/pidp8i.rc
operator configuration (console manager, paths)
.TP
.B /usr/lib/systemd/user/pidp8i.service
the user unit this script controls
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pidp8i-sim (1),
.BR pdp8 (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR screen (1)
